class: runtime
profiles: standard
summary: a line numberer reads standard input through core/io's line reader and a 32-byte buffer and writes each line after its number right-aligned in six columns through a buffered writer, reading \r\n as \n, keeping an empty line and an unterminated last one, and numbering a line too long for its buffer with a note in its place before going on with the next
program: main.ldn
root: ../../../../..
stdin: input.txt
run_expect: output.txt
stream: output
status: 0
constructs: 0570, 0790, 0800, 0900, 0940, 0960, 1100, 1130, 1290, 1650, 1660, 1680
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, macos-arm64, freebsd-x86-64, freebsd-arm64, linux-rv64
